pve-bcachefs (0.1.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Take over the copy_volume virtual-xattr filter from
    pct-move-volume-snapshots. bcachefs lists its IO options through listxattr
    in two namespaces, and every other filesystem rejects both with EOPNOTSUPP,
    so rsync -X aborts with exit 23 and moving a container off bcachefs fails.
    Both are now filtered.
  * The filter belongs here, not in pct-move-volume-snapshots: it is needed
    with stock pve-container and fixes nothing for any other filesystem.
  * Container and VM migration accept bcachefs volumes. Both paths decide
    whether a local volume can move from a hardcoded list of storage types that
    no third-party plugin can join, so any bcachefs guest failed with "storage
    type 'bcachefs' not supported". Nothing was missing from the plugin - PVE
    already exports a subvolume as tar+size - the export path was never
    reached. Both sites carry upstream's TODO saying the check belongs in the
    storage layer.
  * `pct create` works on a bcachefs storage again. pct and qm run Perl with
    -T, where a path from storage.cfg is tainted and syscall(2) refuses it,
    while pvedaemon does not - so the CLI died with "Insecure dependency in
    syscall" while the API and web UI worked. Every path handed to a raw
    syscall is now validated and untainted, not just the one that failed first.
  * Only the project-quota path reached that syscall, so `qm` and the
    raw-image fallback were unaffected. Part of why it went unnoticed.
  * The test suite drove PVE through pvesh alone, so a hundred passing tests
    said nothing about the command line. It now also creates a container with
    `pct` and a disk with `qm`.
  * Continuous testing against a two-node cluster built from scratch under
    QEMU, via pve-storage-lab, with the plugin compiled from the working tree
    on every push: 108 passing, 3 declared limitations.
  * Known limitations are declared rather than skipped, so each still runs and
    is reported the day it starts passing: a container's df shows the
    filesystem rather than its quota, a guest with snapshots cannot migrate,
    and bcachefs logs one failed data read per QEMU open of a VM image.
  * The patch script is patch-pve.pl, not patch-pve-container.pl: it spans
    three files across pve-container and qemu-server. Pristine copies are kept
    under flattened names, since two of them are Migrate.pm and LXC.pm in
    different directories.
  * patch-pve.pl carries a series rather than a single change, applying and
    reverting each independently, and adopts the filter if an older
    pct-move-volume-snapshots already applied it.

 -- Julius Arkenberg <julius@rkenberg.de>  Sun, 13 Sep 2026 15:39:13 +0200

